menu "Bento"

    config BENTO_DEBUG_INTERFACE
        bool "Debug interface over USB (development only)"
        default n
        help
            The test harness talks to the firmware over USB Serial/JTAG (hal_debug_read and hal_debug_write).
            It can do anything, including unlock a locked board and dump what's on screen, for whoever has a USB
            cable: never use it in the firmware you live with. With it off, the firmware never reads USB input.
            tools/bento build|flash <board> --debug turns it on for one build, in firmware/build-<board>-debug,
            without changing the sdkconfig.

    config BENTO_HW_TEST
        bool "Run the hardware test instead of the UX"
        default n
        help
            platform/esp32/hw_test.c: a color pattern, touch dots, a knob counter, feedback on input, and a log of
            Bluetooth and motion. For bring-up of a new board. tools/bento build <board> --hw-test does the same
            without changing the sdkconfig.

endmenu
